asset:        filmagic-color-panel.png
title:        README: color grading panel
author:       Filmagic contributors (screenshot); film/footage/music credits below
source:       original work (screenshot of Filmagic captured with its ui.screenshot control command)
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0 (screenshot); embedded film frames are public domain
license-file:
added:        2026-11-12 by @vansyson1308
notes:        Crop (680x1564 px at 2x) of the Color Grading panel on the first Charade (1963) shot of the Charade - Grade sequence: Basic Correction (temperature and tint sliders with coloured tracks, saturation and light controls), collapsed Creative and Curves sections, Color Wheels & Match open on the shadow, midtone and highlight wheels and the start of the Color Match controls (the HSL Secondary and Vignette sections are below the crop), and the section switches. Shows panel controls only, no film frames. All UI icons are drawn in code; fonts are Inter and JetBrains Mono (OFL-1.1). Contains no Adobe artwork. Rebuild and recapture with the scripts in docs/images/scripts/ (README there): build_trailer.py, then capture_gallery.py color-panel.
Media visible or used in the screenshot (none of it is committed to the repository):
  - Charade (1963), dir. Stanley Donen, Universal. US public domain (defective copyright notice). Source: https://archive.org/details/charade-1963-cary-grant-audrey-hepburn-comedy-mystery-romance-thriller-full-movie (Public Domain Mark).
